<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marcus Aemilius Lepidus (triumvir)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 89–13 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marcus Aemilius Lepidus was a Roman politician and ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a> who formed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-triumvirate">Second Triumvirate</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a> and Octavian in 43 BCE. He was given <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> to govern, but after trying to take <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> from Octavian in 36 BCE he was stripped of his powers. He kept the office of pontifex maximus until his death in 13 or 12 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marcus-aemilius-lepidus-triumvir.jpg" alt="Marcus Aemilius Lepidus (triumvir)" width="320" height="290" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Denarius_of_Lepidus_and_Octavian_(obverse).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
